/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 98 0 R
/T (SEXUAL REPRODUCTIVE HEALTH AND RIGHT  - SRHR Life Skills Sessions)
/E (SEXUAL REPRODUCTIVE HEALTH AND RIGHT  - SRHR Life Skills Sessions)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 98 0 R
/T (In March 2026, the HARAF SRHR team, in collaboration with community PALS facilitators, successfully implemented a series of life skills sessions for adolescents and parents across five intervention communities Fufore, Gurin, Girei 1 & 2, and Jabi Lamba through the Conrad N. Hilton Funded Project. The sessions were strategically designed to equip participants with the knowledge, attitudes, and skills required to make informed decisions for improved health, wellbeing, and positive family relationships.)
/E (In March 2026, the HARAF SRHR team, in collaboration with community PALS facilitators, successfully implemented a series of life skills sessions for adolescents and parents across five intervention communities Fufore, Gurin, Girei 1 & 2, and Jabi Lamba through the Conrad N. Hilton Funded Project. The sessions were strategically designed to equip participants with the knowledge, attitudes, and skills required to make informed decisions for improved health, wellbeing, and positive family relationships.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 98 0 R
/T (Across four progressive PALS sessions, both adolescents and parents actively engaged in structured, participatory learning modules. Adolescents were supported to build self-awareness, understand their social support networks, recognize and manage emotions, and develop positive coping strategies for stress. These sessions created safe spaces that encouraged open dialogue, peer learning, and confidence building.)
/E (Across four progressive PALS sessions, both adolescents and parents actively engaged in structured, participatory learning modules. Adolescents were supported to build self-awareness, understand their social support networks, recognize and manage emotions, and develop positive coping strategies for stress. These sessions created safe spaces that encouraged open dialogue, peer learning, and confidence building.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 98 0 R
/T (For parents and caregivers, the sessions strengthened parenting capacity through practical guidance on stress management, self-care, understanding adolescent development, and adopting positive communication and support strategies. Participants gained critical insights into the physical, emotional, and social needs of adolescents, particularly within challenging and crisis-affected contexts.)
/E (For parents and caregivers, the sessions strengthened parenting capacity through practical guidance on stress management, self-care, understanding adolescent development, and adopting positive communication and support strategies. Participants gained critical insights into the physical, emotional, and social needs of adolescents, particularly within challenging and crisis-affected contexts.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 98 0 R
/T (The sessions recorded strong participation and engagement, with participants demonstrating enthusiasm, sharing experiences, and applying practical skills through interactive activities, a total of 200 participants were reached, including 100 adolescents \(41 Male, 59 Female\) and 100 parents \(27 Male, 73 Female\). Overall, the intervention established a solid foundation for improved adolescent wellbeing, strengthened caregiver support systems, and enhanced family cohesion within the target communities.)
/E (The sessions recorded strong participation and engagement, with participants demonstrating enthusiasm, sharing experiences, and applying practical skills through interactive activities, a total of 200 participants were reached, including 100 adolescents \(41 Male, 59 Female\) and 100 parents \(27 Male, 73 Female\). Overall, the intervention established a solid foundation for improved adolescent wellbeing, strengthened caregiver support systems, and enhanced family cohesion within the target communities.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
