289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (As part of sustained efforts to improve maternal and child health outcomes, HARAF successfully delivered targeted health and nutrition education sessions at Runjin Sambo Primary Health Centre \(PHC\). The intervention effectively engaged both newly registered and returning ANC clients, driving increased early ANC uptake, improved adherence to care schedules, and strengthened adoption of positive maternal health practices.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The sessions provided comprehensive guidance on the importance of consistent use of pregnancy supplements, early ANC registration, and timely reporting of complications. Participants were equipped with practical knowledge on balanced nutrition, emphasizing the intake of protein, fruits, and vegetables essential for healthy maternal and fetal development. Preventive health measures, including the consistent use of insecticide-treated nets \(ITNs\) and improved hygiene and sanitation practices, were strongly reinforced to reduce health risks.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (In addition, the sessions promoted proactive health-seeking behavior, encouraging pregnant women to promptly access care at the PHC when experiencing any discomfort or warning signs during pregnancy.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
