/E (In March 2026, HARAF funded by PROPCOM+ through Community Animal Health Workers \(CAHWs\) and Veterinary Paraprofessionals \(VPPs\) successfully delivered critical livestock health services to approximately 14,985 smallholder poultry and livestock farmers across targeted communities in Adamawa State. Through coordinated outreach, these frontline animal health workers expanded access to essential veterinary interventions, strengthening livestock productivity and household resilience.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
417 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 106 0 R
/E (Operating across key LGAs including Ganye, Guyuk, Gombi, Girei, Fufore, Madagali, Numan, Lamurde, Mubi North, Mubi South, Yola North, and Yola South, about 60 trained animal health personnel ensured sustained community-level service delivery.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 106 0 R
/E (Key interventions included the administration of priority vaccines such as Newcastle Disease \(NCD\) for poultry, Peste des Petits Ruminants \(PPR\) for small ruminants, and Contagious Bovine Pleuropneumonia \(CBPP\) for cattle. In addition, farmers benefited from a comprehensive package of animal health services including treatment of sick animals, wound management, castration, dehorning, debeaking, and routine advisory support on improved husbandry practices.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
