482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (In March 2026, the SRHR team in Adamawa conducted a social marketing distribution at Jabbi/Lamba PHCC, providing essential sexual and reproductive health commodities to adolescents and young people. Items distributed included sanitary pads, towels, cotton wool, gloves, soap, and syringe/needle sets. The intervention aimed to improve access to essential SRH supplies, strengthen hygiene practices, and promote safe, informed health behaviors among young people.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (Throughout March 2026, acoss Adamawa and Borno adolescents and youths in Girei, Malabu, Jabbi Lamba, Ribadu, Alkaleri, Simari and Kaleri communities continued to access a comprehensive package of youth-friendly SRH services through supported PHC facilities. Services included antenatal care, safe deliveries and postnatal care, family planning, STI management, and psychosocial counselling reaching a total of 4073 \(1515 girls, 1870 women, 270 boys and 418 men\).)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (These services were delivered by trained health workers under the Adolescents and Youth Friendly Health Services \(AYFHS\) model, supported by Plan International and HARAF, ensuring a safe, confidential, and responsive environment for young clients.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (The intervention strengthened access to quality SRH services, improved health-seeking behavior among adolescents and youths, and contributed to enhanced awareness and uptake of family planning, STI prevention, and maternal health services across the supported communities.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
