1777 0 obj
<<
/Title (Across four progressive PALS sessions, both adolescents and parents actively engaged in structured, participatory learning modules. Adolescents were supported to build self-awareness, understand their social support networks, recognize and manage emotions, and develop positive coping strategies for stress. These sessions created safe spaces that encouraged open dialogue, peer learning, and confidence building.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1758 0 R
/Prev 1770 0 R
/Next 1779 0 R
>>
endobj
1778 0 obj
<<
/Title (The sessions recorded strong participation and engagement, with participants demonstrating enthusiasm, sharing experiences, and applying practical skills through interactive activities, a total of 200 participants were reached, including 100 adolescents \(41 Male, 59 Female\) and 100 parents \(27 Male, 73 Female\). Overall, the intervention established a solid foundation for improved adolescent wellbeing, strengthened caregiver support systems, and enhanced family cohesion within the target communities.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1758 0 R
/Prev 1779 0 R
/Next 1771 0 R
>>
endobj
1779 0 obj
<<
/Title (For parents and caregivers, the sessions strengthened parenting capacity through practical guidance on stress management, self-care, understanding adolescent development, and adopting positive communication and support strategies. Participants gained critical insights into the physical, emotional, and social needs of adolescents, particularly within challenging and crisis-affected contexts.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1758 0 R
/Prev 1777 0 R
/Next 1778 0 R
>>
endobj
